# What the @@Engine@@ adapter verifies - the source of truth for the engine capability matrix
# (docs-site: reference/engine-capabilities, generated by `./dev/capabilities`) and what the
# verification pipeline consults when a contract relies on something an adapter can't check.
#
# Every capability in verification-core's `Capability` vocabulary must be declared here
# (AdapterCapabilities.parse refuses a file that leaves one out): an adapter that cannot do
# something says so, with a reason. Anything other than `supported` needs a `note`.
#
# Generated with every capability `unsupported` - the safe default, which makes a contract that relies on
# one fail with UNSUPPORTED_CONTRACT_FEATURE instead of passing unchecked. Move a capability to `supported`
# or `partial` only when the engine investigation (docs/ADDING_AN_ENGINE_ADAPTER.md) has a finding for it
# AND the conformance kit passes its scenarios; the kit holds a declaration to what it says.
adapter: @@engine@@
engine: @@Engine@@
enforcement:
  # TODO(engine investigation, question 1): in-engine-blocking, pre-submit-gate or observe-only.
  point: observe-only
  note: >-
    Not yet investigated: where @@Engine@@ can be gated has not been decided.
capabilities:
@@CAPABILITIES@@
